   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>The documentation on htmlwidgets has improved since the last time I checked. These is especially a very usefull post from deanattali.</div><div><br></div><div><div><a href=\"http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391106840000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2JZIq2EZZ9_fqTAd1AeC3r\">http://www.htmlwidgets.org/develop_intro.html</a></div><div><a href=\"http://deanattali.com/blog/htmlwidgets-tips/#widget-to-r-data\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://deanattali.com/blog/htmlwidgets-tips/%23widget-to-r-data&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792391106840000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2P57V5SgglwDCd5209Dltr\">http://deanattali.com/blog/htmlwidgets-tips/#widget-to-r-data</a></div></div><div><br></div><div>My workaround is to use a custom widget using htmlwidgets. The widget manages the creation/deletion of input fields and send the inputs as one json message to the server side. For Shiny, this means that there is only one input  so there&#39;s no more problem.</div><div><br></div><div>Vincent</div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
